From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:47:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure recent header-time persistence diagnostics

Expose unsigned header counts, raw missing-index block hashes, paths and
errors for five existing Info sites. Preserve readable punctuation, file
version/bytes, commit/rename operations, update loops and the opt-in default.
A focused walletless control proposes genesis-only dump, twenty-block dump,
then owned missing-index and truncated diagnostic files. It checks unchanged
tip/height and clean restarts before inspecting actual fields. Runtime and
rare dump commit/rename failures remain explicitly pending/unforced.

